 Then I sold it to a bunch of creators who also went viral with it.

7
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:25,560
 So here is the storytelling framework. Comment story if you want the full thing.

8
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:27,420
 Starting off with a relatable hook. Here's an example.

9
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:31,020
 The past month, I have been in one of the biggest slums of my life. I procrastinated all of my work.

10
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:38,320
 On the fundamental level, all you need to do with your hook in your first three seconds of your video is just stop their school and make them feel an emotion so that you get prompted to keep watching.

11
00:00:38,380 --> 00:00:41,400
 The next four sentences is where actual storytelling comes in.

12
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:44,980
 One year ago, I promised my mom I'd hit this crazy goal. She let me drop down and pursue my dream of content creation.

13
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:52,080
 And against all Asian parent will, on January 1st, 2024, the goal of your backstory is to be as specific as possible with numbers, dates, places.

14
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:56,480
 And be vulnerable because if you are the hero of your own story, you can't just be a winner from day one.

15
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:59,460
 I like to describe your backstory as if you're going through a deep conflict.

16
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:01,880
 Stage three of five is so important. I call it a breaking point.

17
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:05,800
 Describe the one moment where everything changed for you.

18
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:07,660
 By stage four, your storytelling is complete.

19
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:11,480
 So now you can just give your takeaway and tell your viewer what the lesson learned is.

20
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:13,540
 Then finally, you can give them a little CTA.

